      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s no dex2oat in `/system/bin`. Therefore, the process probably gets SIGABRT rather than SIGKILL.\n\nI recommend to test with something that exists in `/system/bin`, preferably long-running, so it has a chance to be killed. I would choose `sleep`.\n\nAlso, this test needs to pass on host as well, so you probably need a function like [this](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android-latest-release:art/runtime/exec_utils_test.cc;l\u003d54-63;drc\u003d6f3beba5e01780c30364e34be15335da51c4e0e5) to find the right binary based on whether it\u0027s on device or host.\n\nIn addition, check `result.signal` at the end, to make sure it is indeed SIGKILL, not something else.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1312,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 1312,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4e1673630a60903de778189fc812bfbebd4b5e7f",
